{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-258", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/258", "wordCount": 2419, "segments": [{"start": 8.0, "text": "My name is Janum Trivedi, and"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "I'm an engineer on the UIKit"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "frameworks team."}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "First, let's talk about"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "architecting your app for"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "multiple windows."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "On iOS 13, supporting multiple"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "windows is a fantastic way to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "make your existing apps more"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "useful and allow your users to"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "be substantially more productive."}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "We'll be going over three"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "primary topics today."}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "We'll get started by doing a"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "quick overview of the changes to"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "the application life cycle that"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "will allow multiple windows on"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "iOS 13 to be possible."}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "Then, we'll dive deeper into the"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "new UIScene delegate and we'll"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "talk about what kind of work you"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "should be doing there."}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "Finally, we'll go over some best"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "practices in ArchitectureKit so"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "you and your team can take"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "advantage of to make sure you"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "provide your users with a"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "consistent, seamless"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "multitasking experience."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "Now, to get started, let's talk"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "about some of the roles and"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "responsibilities of the App"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "Delegate in iOS 12 and before."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "The App Delegate had two primary"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "roles."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "The first was to notify your"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "application of process level"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "events."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "So, the system would notify your"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "App Delegate when your process"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "was launching or was about to"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "terminate."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "But it also had the second role,"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "which was letting your"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "application know the state of"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "its UI."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "So, via some methods like did"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "enter foreground and will resign"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "active, the system will let you"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "know your UI state."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "And this is totally fine in iOS"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "12 and before, because"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "applications had one process and"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "also just one user interface"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "instance to match it."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "So, today your App Delegate"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "probably looks a little bit"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "something like this, except"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "maybe not quite this short."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "So, in your did finish launching"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "with options, you do a couple"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "things. First you do some one-time"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "non-UI global setup, like"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "connecting to a database or"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "initializing your data"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "structures."}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "And immediately after that, you"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "set up your user interface."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "And again, this is totally valid"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "in 12 and before, but iOS 13's"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "pattern is invalid."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "Why? Because applications now"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "still just share one process but"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "may have multiple user interface"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "instances or scene sessions."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "That means the responsibility of"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "the App Delegate needs to change"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "a bit."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "It's still responsible for"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "process events and life cycle,"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "but it's no longer responsible"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "for anything related to your UI"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "lifecycle."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Instead, that'll all be handled"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "by your UIScene Delegate."}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "Well, what does that mean for"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "you?"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "Any UI setup or teardown work"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "that you used to do in your App"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "Delegate now needs to migrate to"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "the corresponding methods in"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "your Scene Delegate."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "In fact, on iOS 13, if your"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "application adopts the new scene"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "lifecycle, UIKit will stop"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "calling the old App Delegate"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "methods that relate to UI state."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "Instead, we'll call the new"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "Scene Delegate methods, and it's"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "pretty simple since there's a"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "1-to-1 mapping for most of"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "these."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "But don't worry - if you want to"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "adopt multiple windows support"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "on iOS 13, that doesn't mean you"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "need to drop support for 12 and"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "before."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "If you're back deploying, you"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "can simply keep both sets of"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "these methods and UIKit will"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "call the correct set at runtime."}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "Now, before we dive into the"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "exact delegate methods, there's"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "one more additional"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "responsibility that the App"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "Delegate gets."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "And that is the system will now"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "notify your App Delegate when a"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "new Scene Session is being"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "created, or an existing Scene"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "Session is being discarded."}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "Let's make this lifecycle a"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "little bit more concrete."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "Say I've been working on this"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "little blue app right here and I"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "want to launch it for the first"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "time."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "Let's go through the call stack."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "First, your App Delegate's going"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "to get the same did finish"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "launching with options call."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "Again, it's still fine to do"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "your one-time non-UI setup here."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "Then immediately after that, the"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "system's going to create a scene"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "But before it creates the actual"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "UI Scene, it's going to ask our"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "application for UIScene"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "configuration."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "This configuration specifies"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "what scene delegate, what story"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "board, and if you specified,"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "what scene subclass you want to"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "create the scene with."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "It's worth noting that you can"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "define these scene"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "configurations either"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "dynamically in code or"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "preferably statically in your"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "info.plist."}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "This also gives you an"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "opportunity to select the right"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "configuration."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "You may have a main scene"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "configuration, and you may have"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "an accessory scene."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "So, you should look at the"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "options parameter that's"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "provided here, to use that as"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "the context to pick the right"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "scene configuration."}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "Once you've defined these, for"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "example in your info.plist, it's"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "really simple. You just refer to it by name,"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "making sure you pass in the role"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "of the incoming sessions role."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "Great."}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "Now our app is launched."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "We have a scene session."}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "But we don't see any UI, and"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "that's where our scene delegates"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "did connect to scene session"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "comes in."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "Let's look at what kind of work"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "we should do here. This is where you set up your UI"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "window with the new designated"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "UI window initializer."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "We'll notice that we pass in the"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "window scene provided."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "But importantly, we need to also"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "check for any relevant user"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "activities or state restoration"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "activities to configure our"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "window with."}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "We'll talk about that more in a"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "second."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "Yay, now we see our app."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "So, what happens when one of our"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "users actually swipes up to go"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "back home?"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "Well, the old familiar will"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "resign active and did enter"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "background methods get called on"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "your scene delegate."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "But, now there's something"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "interesting."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "At some point in time after,"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "your scene may be disconnected."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "Well, what does that mean?"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "Well, in order to reclaim"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "resources, the system may at"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "some point after your scene"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "enters the background, release"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "that scene from memory."}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "That also means your scene"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "delegate will be released from"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "memory and any window"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "hierarchies or view hierarchies"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "held by your scene delegate will"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "be released as well."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "This gives you an opportunity to"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "deallocate and release any large"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "resources in memory that were"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "retained by somewhere else in"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "your application that related to"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "this scene."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "But it's important to not use"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "this to actually delete any"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "user data or state permanently,"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "as the scene may reconnect and"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "return later."}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "But then let's talk about what"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "actually happens when our user"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "actually swipes up on a scene"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "session on switch and explicitly"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "wants to destroy it?"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "Well, the system will call our"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "App Delegates didDiscardSceneSessions."}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "This finally gives us an"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "opportunity to actually"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "permanently delegate any user"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "state or data associated with"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "the scene such as an unsaved"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "draft in a text editing app."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "Now, it's also possible that one"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "of your users removed one or"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "more UIScenes from the switcher"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "by swiping up while your actual"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "app process was not running."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "If your process was not running,"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "the system will keep track of"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "the discarded sessions and call"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "this shortly after your"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "application's next launch."}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "Now, let's talk about some"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "architecture patters that you"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "can consider integrating into"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "your apps."}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "We'll start by talking about"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "state restoration."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "In iOS 13, state restoration is"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "no longer a nicety."}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "It is crucial for your"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "application to implement"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "scene-based state restoration."}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "Let's go over why that is."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "Here's our app switcher."}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "I have a document app and I'm"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "planning a road trip and I have"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "four different sessions of"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "different documents open right"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "now."}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "But I'm really focusing on"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "packing list and agenda."}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "At some point, these other two"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "backgrounded road trip and"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "attendee scenes, have been"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "disconnected and released by the"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "If I don't implement state"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "restoration here, when I go back"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "to the road trip, I'm not going"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "to return to the state that I"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "was previously in."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "I'm not going to scene the"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "document that I was editing."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Instead, I'll just start over,"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "like it's a brand-new window,"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "and that's not a great user"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "Well, how can we resolve this?"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "iOS 13 has a brand-new"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "scene-based state restoration"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "API."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "And it's super simple."}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "It works by not any more"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "encoding view hierarchies, but"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "instead just encoding the state"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "which will allow you to recreate"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "your window."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "This is all based on NSUser"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "activity as well. So, if your application"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "leverages powerful technologies"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "like spotlight search or"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "handoff, you can use these same"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "activities to encode the state"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "of your app."}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "It's also worth noting that in"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "iOS 13, the state restoration"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "archive that you give back to"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "the system will match the same"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "data protection class of the"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "rest of your application."}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "What does this look like in"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "code? Well, in our scene delegate, we"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "implement state restoration"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "activity for scene and then I"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "call a method that finds the"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "most active relevant user"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "activity form in the current"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "window."}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "Then we return that."}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "After some time, when that scene"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "re-enters the foreground and"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "becomes connected, we check if"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "the session contains a state"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "restoration activity."}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "If it does, we use that"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "activity."}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "If not, we can create a"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "brand-new window without any"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "state."}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "This means that no matter what,"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "our users will never notice when"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "scenes get disconnected in the"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "background because they"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "shouldn't."}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "Finally, let's talk about one"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "more important issue that you"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "may run into when adopting"}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "support for multiple windows."}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "And that is how to best keep"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "application scenes in sync."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "Let me make this more concrete."}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "I've been working on a new chat"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "application right here, and as"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "we see, I just recently added"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "support for multiple windows on"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "iOS 13."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "And I have a chat with my"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "friend, Giovanni, who will join"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "me on stage in a couple minutes,"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "and notice that we're viewing"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "the same conversation in two"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "different view controllers and"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "two different scenes at the same"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "time."}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "So, let's say I want to send"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "Giovanni a message and let him"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "know I'm ready for lunch."}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "Oh, only one of our scenes"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "updated."}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "So, why is that?"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "Well, it turns out that on iOS,"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "a lot of apps are structured in"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "this kind of way in which view"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "controllers receive an event,"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "maybe via button tap, me"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "pressing the send button."}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "And then the view controller"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "itself updates its own UI."}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "After that, our view controller"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "notifies our model or model"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "controller."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "And this is mostly okay when we"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "just are talking about one user"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "interface instance."}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "But now if we introduce a second"}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "view controller in a different"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "scene that's showing the same"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "data, at no point is this new"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "view controller being notified"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "to update itself with this new"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "data."}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "That's an issue."}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "Well, we can resolve this."}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "Architecturally, now if our view"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "controllers, upon receiving an"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "event, immediately and only"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "notify our model controller,"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "then we can have our model"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "controller actually notify any"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "relevant subscribers or view"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "controllers, telling them that"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "they should update with this new"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "data."}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "There are a number of ways that"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "we can do this."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "We can use delegates,"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "notifications."}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "We can even use the fantastic"}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "new Swift Combine framework"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "released this year."}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "But let's go over a lightweight"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "Swift example that you can"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "consider integrating into your"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "apps."}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "Here's the current method that"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "gets called when I press the"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "return button on sending a"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "message."}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "We create a message model"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "My view controller updates its"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "own views."}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "And then we notify our model"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "controller to persist this."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "And the first thing we need to"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "do is this view controller"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "should not be mutating its own"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "view state."}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "Instead, we're just going to get"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "rid of that code. We'll add that back later in a"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "second."}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "Now, let's look at what that"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "model controller add method is"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "actually doing."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "It's pretty simple."}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "All we're doing is persisting"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "that new message."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "But we actually want the model"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "controller to now notify if any"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "other view controllers or"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "connected scenes that there has"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "been an update."}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "How are we going to send this"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "update down?"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "We want a structured way to"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "package this event such that"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "it's strongly typed and it's"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "easily debuggable and testable."}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "So, let's go ahead and actually"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "create a new type and we'll call"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "it update event."}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "It's a Swift enum with"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "associated values."}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "So, we'll add a new message"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "type."}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "This is the object that our"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "model controller is going to"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "create on receiving a new"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "message and will then send down"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "to any relevant view controllers"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "or scenes."}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "Because we want to post this,"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "we'll use NSNotification center"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "as the backing store for this."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "So, we'll add this handy post"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "method that lets us in one line"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "create a new update event and"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "then post it to any subscribers."}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "The implementation is fairly"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "straightforward."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "We just post a notification to"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "the new message notification"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "name channel."}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "But the trick here is that we're"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "including the update event"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "object itself in the"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "notifications object."}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "This will come in handy, as"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "we'll see in a second."}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "Now, when our model controller"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "is notified that a new message"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "was added, after we persist it,"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "we can just create this new"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "event and call post."}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "Then, if we look at how we have"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "to change our view controllers,"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "we observe this new event."}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "In this case, the new message"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "notification name."}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "And then we create a handler"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "method that we get the"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "notification from in the arguments."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "And remember, when we pass the"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "update event as the"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "notifications object, we can now"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "pull that event right back out"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "from the notification."}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "Then, we can easily switch on"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "the kind of case of the event"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "and because we created an"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "associated enum, we can pull the"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "message out."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "Now, we can update our user"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "interface here."}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "So, let's see what happens when"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "I send Giovanni that same"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "message after implementing this"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "new architecture."}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "Hey! All of our scenes update."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "So, we've gone over a lot today."}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "We've gone over some of the differences in the app versus"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "scene delegate and the"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "differences in responsibilities."}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "We've also gone over some of the"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "major scene delegate methods and"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "what kind of work you should do"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "there."}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "We also talked about why state"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "restoration is so crucial for"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "you to use on iOS 13 and how you"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "can leverage the new scene-based"}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "API to do so."}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "Finally, we talked about some"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "high-level patterns for creating"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "a one-way data flow such that we"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "can keep all of our scenes in"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "sync while they share the same"}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "data."}]}
